IMPORT prelude

-- Nanyang Polytechnic Act 1992 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a student, a donor, a business contracting with the
-- Polytechnic, or a member of its Board: execution of instruments under the common seal (s 4(2)), fees and the validation of
-- late-payment charges (ss 5(2)(c), 5A), who may be awarded a diploma (s 12; Schedule s 11(g)), who may end a student's studies
-- (Schedule ss 6(3)(c), 11(j)), when regulations take effect (Schedule ss 6(4), 12(2)), the size, terms, quorum and voting of the
-- Board (Schedule ss 5, 8, 9), the Senate's quorum (Schedule s 10(3)), donations (Schedule ss 16, 17), the Students' Union and the
-- Societies Act (s 15) and the financial year (Schedule s 14).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 1/4/2024"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/NPA1992.txt. The deposit says the revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including
-- 1 December 2021"; the latest annotation is "[Act 4 of 2008 wef 01/04/2024]" against ss 5(2)(c), 5A and Schedule s 6(2)(k), (3)(f).
-- The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step with the body by one number; the BODY's numbering is followed.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0186 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. SCOPED to the provisions such a person meets. Not encoded: incorporation and objects beyond the fee power
-- (ss 3, 5), the Schools (s 7), committees and delegation (s 8), appointment of officers and staff (s 9, Schedule ss 2 to 4), the
-- Minister's power to amend the Constitution (s 10), grants-in-aid (s 13), shares to the Minister for Finance (s 14), the Board's
-- and Senate's lists of powers beyond the points above, estimates (Schedule s 15) and the Students' Union fee (Schedule s 18(3)).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Nanyang Polytechnic Act 1992`

§§ `4(2) -- execution under the common seal`

-- s 4(2): instruments requiring the seal "must be sealed with the common seal of the Polytechnic and the instruments to which the
-- common seal is affixed must be signed by the Principal or a Deputy Principal and by another member of the Board."
-- Schedule s 5(1): the Board is a Chairperson, a Deputy Chairperson, the Principal and 9 to 15 others appointed by the Minister. A
-- Deputy Principal and the Registrar are not members as such (INFERENCE from s 5(1); either may be appointed a member, and is then
-- an appointed member here).
DECLARE Signatory IS ONE OF
    `the Principal`
    `a Deputy Principal`
    `the Chairperson`
    `an appointed Board member`
    `the Registrar`

GIVEN `the signer` IS A Signatory
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may sign first` IF
    CONSIDER `the signer`
    WHEN `the Principal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Deputy Principal` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the signer` IS A Signatory
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a member of the Board` IF
    CONSIDER `the signer`
    WHEN `the Principal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Chairperson` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an appointed Board member` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the signer` IS A Signatory
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the Principal` IF
    CONSIDER `the signer`
    WHEN `the Principal` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "another member": the second signer must be a Board member other than the first signer.
GIVEN `sealed` IS A BOOLEAN, `first signer` IS A Signatory, `second signer` IS A Signatory
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument is duly executed under seal` IF
        `sealed`
    AND `may sign first` `first signer`
    AND `is a member of the Board` `second signer`
    AND (NOT (`is the Principal` `first signer` AND `is the Principal` `second signer`))

§§ `5(2)(c) and 5A -- fees and late-payment charges`

-- s 5(2)(c): the Polytechnic may "fix, demand and receive fees and other charges, including charges for the late payment of any
-- such fee or charge".
-- s 5A: "Every amount collected before the date of commencement of the Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2008 as, or
-- purportedly as, a charge for the late payment of any fee or charge referred to in section 5(2)(c) shall be deemed to be and always
-- to have been validly collected, and no legal proceedings shall lie or be instituted or maintained in any court of law on account of
-- or in respect of any such collection." The deposit does not give that Act's commencement date, so it is taken as a fact.
GIVEN `collected as a late-payment charge` IS A BOOLEAN, `collected before the 2008 Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `proceedings over the collection are barred` IF
    `collected as a late-payment charge` AND `collected before the 2008 Act commenced`

§§ `12 and Schedule s 11(g) -- diplomas and certificates`

-- s 12: power "(a) to award diplomas and certificates and any other academic distinctions specified in regulations made under the
-- Constitution; and (b) to provide such lectures and instruction for persons who are not registered students ... and to award
-- diplomas, certificates and other academic distinctions to those persons."
-- Schedule s 11(g): the Senate decides "persons who are qualified for the award of diplomas, certificates and other marks of
-- distinction". (Joining s 12 to s 11(g) as a single condition is an INFERENCE.)
GIVEN `is a registered student` IS A BOOLEAN, `took Polytechnic instruction as a non-registered person` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Senate decided the person is qualified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Polytechnic may award the person a diploma` IF
        (`is a registered student` OR `took Polytechnic instruction as a non-registered person`)
    AND `the Senate decided the person is qualified`

§§ `Schedule ss 6(3)(c), 11(j) -- ending a student's studies`

-- Schedule s 11(j): the Senate may "require any student on academic grounds to terminate his or her studies at the Polytechnic".
-- Schedule s 6(3)(c): the BOARD may by regulations provide for "the welfare, discipline, suspension and expulsion of students".
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `academic grounds`
    `misconduct`

DECLARE Route IS ONE OF
    `the Senate may require it directly`
    `expulsion under the Board's regulations`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A Route
`the route to ending the student's studies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `academic grounds` THEN `the Senate may require it directly`
    OTHERWISE `expulsion under the Board's regulations`

§§ `Schedule ss 6(4), 12(2) -- when regulations take effect`

-- Schedule s 6(4): Board regulations "come into operation on the day on which they are made unless otherwise provided by the Board."
-- Schedule s 12(2): Senate regulations "must be reported to the Board and come into operation not earlier than one semester after the
-- day on which they are made, unless otherwise approved by the Board."
DECLARE Maker IS ONE OF
    `the Board`
    `the Senate`

DECLARE Commencement IS ONE OF
    `on the day it is made`
    `not earlier than one semester after it is made`
    `as the Board provides or approves`

GIVEN `the maker` IS A Maker, `the Board has provided or approved otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Commencement
`when the regulation comes into operation` MEANS
    IF `the Board has provided or approved otherwise`
    THEN `as the Board provides or approves`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the maker`
         WHEN `the Board` THEN `on the day it is made`
         OTHERWISE `not earlier than one semester after it is made`

§§ `Schedule ss 5, 8 -- the Board's size and terms`

-- Schedule s 5(1): Chairperson, Deputy Chairperson, the Principal, and "such other persons, not being less than 9 or more than 15, as
-- the Minister may determine". (2): every member except the Principal is appointed by the Minister and, "unless the Minister otherwise
-- directs, holds office for a period of 3 years" and is eligible for re-appointment.
-- s 8: a person filling a vacancy "must be appointed for the remainder of the term of the person's predecessor".
GIVEN `other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the number of other members is lawful` IF
    `other members` AT LEAST 9 AND `other members` AT MOST 15

GIVEN `other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the size of the Board` MEANS
    `other members` PLUS 3

GIVEN `fills a vacancy` IS A BOOLEAN, `predecessor's remaining years` IS A NUMBER, `the Minister directs otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN, `directed years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the term of the appointment in years` MEANS
    IF `fills a vacancy` THEN `predecessor's remaining years`
    ELSE IF `the Minister directs otherwise` THEN `directed years`
         ELSE 3

§§ `Schedule s 9 -- Board meetings`

-- Schedule s 9(2): "The quorum at every meeting of the Board is 6 members." (3): decisions "by a simple majority of the votes of the
-- members present and voting except that, in the case of an equality of votes, the Chairperson or, in his or her absence, the Deputy
-- Chairperson has a casting vote." (5): if both are absent, a member elected by those present presides -- and the text gives that
-- member NO casting vote.
GIVEN `present` IS A NUMBER, `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `the Chairperson or Deputy Chairperson is present` IS A BOOLEAN, `the casting vote is for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board resolution is carried` IF
        `present` AT LEAST 6
    AND (    `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`
         OR  (`votes for` EQUALS `votes against` AND `the Chairperson or Deputy Chairperson is present` AND `the casting vote is for`))

§§ `Schedule s 10(3) -- Senate quorum`

-- Schedule s 10(3): "The quorum at every meeting of the Senate is one-quarter of the total number of members of the Senate."
GIVEN `present` IS A NUMBER, `total members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Senate meeting is quorate` IF
    `present` TIMES 4 AT LEAST `total members`

§§ `Schedule ss 16, 17 -- donations`

-- Schedule s 16(2): "Records must be kept of all donations to the Polytechnic including the names of donors and any special
-- conditions". s 17: property donated "for any specific purpose must be applied and administered in accordance with the purpose ...
-- and must be separately accounted for."
GIVEN `donor and conditions recorded` IS A BOOLEAN, `given for a specific purpose` IS A BOOLEAN, `applied to that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN, `separately accounted for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the donation is handled as the Constitution requires` IF
        `donor and conditions recorded`
    AND ((NOT `given for a specific purpose`) OR (`applied to that purpose` AND `separately accounted for`))

§§ `15 -- the Students' Union and the Societies Act`

-- s 15(1): "Despite anything to the contrary in the Societies Act 1966, the provisions of that Act apply to the Nanyang Polytechnic
-- Students' Union and its constituent bodies". (2): the Minister for societies may by order exempt the Union or a constituent body
-- "from all or any of the provisions ... subject to any conditions specified in the order".
GIVEN `exempted from the provision by order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Societies Act provision binds the Students' Union` IF
    NOT `exempted from the provision by order`

§§ `Schedule s 14 -- financial year`

-- Schedule s 14: "The financial year of the Polytechnic begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year."
-- Result: the calendar year in which the financial year containing the date began.
GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER, `year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the financial year beginning in` MEANS
    IF `month` AT LEAST 4 THEN `year` ELSE `year` MINUS 1
